  "question": {
    "text": "<p>To check the principle of multiple proportions, a series of pure binary compounds <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;were analysed and their composition is tabulated below. The correct option(s) is(are)</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 400px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Compound</strong></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Weight <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math></strong></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Weight <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math></strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>44</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "If empirical formula of compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, then the empirical formula of compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "If empirical formula of compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and atomic weight of element <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> , then the atomic weight of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>.</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
